WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:05.525
A passenger leans over the rail to see a fish, the boat lurches, and he’s gone.

2
00:00:05.775 --> 00:00:09.725
What you do in the next ten seconds decides how this ends.

3
00:00:09.975 --> 00:00:12.125
So let’s make it automatic.

4
00:00:12.375 --> 00:00:15.975
Shout man overboard, point at him, and keep pointing.

5
00:00:16.225 --> 00:00:18.375
Throw flotation right now.

6
00:00:18.625 --> 00:00:21.900
A ring buoy, a cushion, anything that floats.

7
00:00:22.150 --> 00:00:25.625
It gives him something to hold, and it marks the spot.

8
00:00:25.875 --> 00:00:28.900
Hit the man overboard button on the GPS.

9
00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:31.875
Turn the boat toward the side he fell from.

10
00:00:32.125 --> 00:00:33.750
Why toward him?

11
00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:39.675
Because turning toward him swings your stern, and your propellers, away from him.

12
00:00:39.925 --> 00:00:46.275
And give one person a single job: eyes and arm on the man in the water, and never look away.

13
00:00:46.525 --> 00:00:53.000
A head in the waves disappears in seconds, and once you’ve lost sight of him, you may not find him again.
